# Code owners (docs/governance.md §1, D-152): who is asked to review a change to a part of the code.
#
# - The first name of a line is who writes the area; the others review it. Every area has at least two, so that the
#   author of a pull request is never its only owner (GitHub does not count an author's approval of their own pull
#   request).
# - The last pattern that matches a file decides its owners, so the general lines come first and the specific ones
#   after. A more specific line replaces the general one for its paths.
# - The QA group's approval of every pull request is a rule of the repository (the owner's setting), not a line here.
#   The group is named below only for the parts of the code that are QA's own.
#
# Alice: architecture, direction, the organisation and management tools. Bob: UI, UX, Qt. Charlie: image processing
# and the GPU. The owner (Patrick) is asked to review what the governance reserves to him: formats, the plugin API,
# the pipeline definition, the write path and the sandbox (docs/governance.md §3); he is on the lines of those areas.

# Everything not named below: the documents, the root files, the decision log, the build; Alice and the owner.
*                                       @straycat-alice-cc @patrickfournier

